<li data-start=3D"696" data-end=3D"715">
<p data-start=3D"698" data-end=3D"715">dewpoint_2m (K)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"716" data-end=3D"741">
<p data-start=3D"718" data-end=3D"741">surface_pressure (Pa)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"742" data-end=3D"769">
<p data-start=3D"744" data-end=3D"769">total_precipitation (m)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"771" data-end=3D"860">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F <strong data-star=
t=3D"774" data-end=3D"788">IMPORTANT:</strong><br data-start=3D"788" data-e=
nd=3D"791">
If you don=E2=80=99t use the correct units, your miner gets heavily punishe=
d.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"862" data-end=3D"865">
<h1 data-start=3D"867" data-end=3D"901">=E2=9C=85 STEP 1 =E2=80=94 Decide t=
he MODEL TYPE</h1>
<p data-start=3D"903" data-end=3D"976">Before I generate the full script, t=
ell me which model you want to train:</p>
<hr data-start=3D"978" data-end=3D"981">
<h2 data-start=3D"983" data-end=3D"1031">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"98=
8" data-end=3D"1029">Option A =E2=80=94 Simple MLP (1-dimensional)</strong>=
</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1032" data-end=3D"1094">Predict the next 6=E2=80=9324 hour=
s for a <strong data-start=3D"1066" data-end=3D"1093">single point (lat, lo=
n)</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1096" data-end=3D"1170">Pros:<br data-start=3D"1101" data-=
end=3D"1104">
=E2=9C=94 Easiest<br data-start=3D"1113" data-end=3D"1116">
=E2=9C=94 Trains on CPU/GPU<br data-start=3D"1135" data-end=3D"1138">
=E2=9C=94 Good to get &gt; 0% performance</p>
<p data-start=3D"1172" data-end=3D"1237">Cons:<br data-start=3D"1177" data-=
end=3D"1180">
=E2=9D=8C Not super strong<br data-start=3D"1198" data-end=3D"1201">
=E2=9D=8C Only works per-station, not global</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1239" data-end=3D"1242">
<h2 data-start=3D"1244" data-end=3D"1287">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"1=
249" data-end=3D"1285">Option B =E2=80=94 Small U-Net (2D grid)</strong></h=
2>
<p data-start=3D"1288" data-end=3D"1363">Train on small 64=C3=9764 or 128=
=C3=97128 tiles from ERA5, predict the next timestep.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1365" data-end=3D"1451">Pros:<br data-start=3D"1370" data-=
end=3D"1373">
=E2=9C=94 MUCH stronger<br data-start=3D"1388" data-end=3D"1391">
=E2=9C=94 Global model<br data-start=3D"1405" data-end=3D"1408">
=E2=9C=94 Good enough to beat Open-Meteo baseline</p>
<p data-start=3D"1453" data-end=3D"1491">Cons:<br data-start=3D"1458" data-=
end=3D"1461">
=E2=9D=8C Needs GPU (L4 / A10G / 3090)</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1493" data-end=3D"1496">
<h2 data-start=3D"1498" data-end=3D"1545">=E2=AD=90 <strong data-start=3D"1=
503" data-end=3D"1543">Option C =E2=80=94 GraphCast-lite (3D model)</strong=
></h2>
