7" data-end=3D"100">
They are a <em data-start=3D"111" data-end=3D"122">core part</em> of how Ze=
us miners and validators work.</p>
<p data-start=3D"164" data-end=3D"201">Let me explain it clearly and simply=
.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"203" data-end=3D"206">
<h1 data-start=3D"208" data-end=3D"238">=E2=9C=85 <strong data-start=3D"212=
" data-end=3D"238">What is a <code data-start=3D"224" data-end=3D"230">.npy=
</code> file?</strong></h1>
<p data-start=3D"239" data-end=3D"286">A <code data-start=3D"241" data-end=
=3D"247">.npy</code> file is a <strong data-start=3D"258" data-end=3D"285">=
NumPy binary array file</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"288" data-end=3D"467">
<li data-start=3D"288" data-end=3D"349">
<p data-start=3D"290" data-end=3D"349">It stores tensors/arrays in a very f=
ast, efficient format</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"350" data-end=3D"392">
<p data-start=3D"352" data-end=3D"392">It loads instantly with <code data-s=
tart=3D"376" data-end=3D"390">numpy.load()</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"393" data-end=3D"467">
<p data-start=3D"395" data-end=3D"408">It preserves:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"467">
<li data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"420">
<p data-start=3D"413" data-end=3D"420">shape</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"423" data-end=3D"432">
<p data-start=3D"425" data-end=3D"432">dtype</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"435" data-end=3D"449">
<p data-start=3D"437" data-end=3D"449">endianness</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"452" data-end=3D"467">
<p data-start=3D"454" data-end=3D"467">array order</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"469" data-end=3D"500">Zeus uses <code data-start=3D"479" d=
ata-end=3D"485">.npy</code> files because:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"502" data-end=3D"696">
<li data-start=3D"502" data-end=3D"547">
<p data-start=3D"504" data-end=3D"547">They are <strong data-start=3D"513" =
data-end=3D"528">much faster</strong> than CSV or JSON</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"548" data-end=3D"602">
<p data-start=3D"550" data-end=3D"602">Easy to share between Python miners =
and validators</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"603" data-end=3D"696">
<p data-start=3D"605" data-end=3D"696">Perfect for storing <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"625" data-end=3D"653">ERA5 ground truth slices</strong>, <strong data=
-start=3D"655" data-end=3D"675">difficulty masks</strong>, <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"677" data-end=3D"690">grid data</strong>, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
