<p data-start=3D"4036" data-end=3D"4065">Each variable is independent:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4067" data-end=3D"4158">
<li data-start=3D"4067" data-end=3D"4086">
<p data-start=3D"4069" data-end=3D"4086">Different units</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4087" data-end=3D"4111">
<p data-start=3D"4089" data-end=3D"4111">Different magnitudes</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4112" data-end=3D"4136">
<p data-start=3D"4114" data-end=3D"4136">Different difficulty</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4137" data-end=3D"4158">
<p data-start=3D"4139" data-end=3D"4158">Different physics</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4160" data-end=3D"4232">If you try to shove all variables =
into one model, your training becomes:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4234" data-end=3D"4316">
<li data-start=3D"4234" data-end=3D"4244">
<p data-start=3D"4236" data-end=3D"4244">Harder</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4245" data-end=3D"4262">
<p data-start=3D"4247" data-end=3D"4262">Less accurate</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4263" data-end=3D"4276">
<p data-start=3D"4265" data-end=3D"4276">Very slow</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4277" data-end=3D"4316">
<p data-start=3D"4279" data-end=3D"4316">Requires multi-channel architectur=
e</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"4318" data-end=3D"4350">Better to specialize each model.</=
p>
<hr data-start=3D"4352" data-end=3D"4355">
<h1 data-start=3D"4357" data-end=3D"4393">=F0=9F=94=A5 FINAL SUMMARY =E2=80=
=94 SUPER IMPORTANT</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"4395" data-end=3D"4440">=E2=9C=94 <code data-start=3D"440=
1" data-end=3D"4413">--variable</code> trains only ONE variable</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4441" data-end=3D"4489">You run the script separately for =
each variable.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4491" data-end=3D"4539">=E2=9C=94 <code data-start=3D"449=
7" data-end=3D"4511">--data-files</code> must be ERA5 NetCDF files</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4540" data-end=3D"4571">Downloaded from Copernicus CDS.</p=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"4573" data-end=3D"4621">=E2=9C=94 You MUST have ERA5 vari=
ables in the file</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4622" data-end=3D"4687">If the ERA5 file contains only tem=
perature, you can't train wind.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4689" data-end=3D"4720">=E2=9C=94 Train 6 separate models=
</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4721" data-end=3D"4774">One model for each Zeus variable y=
ou want to support.</p>
