<p data-start=3D"81" data-end=3D"238">Short answer:<br data-start=3D"94" da=
ta-end=3D"97">
=F0=9F=91=89 <strong data-start=3D"100" data-end=3D"157">Training from 2020=
 is totally fine, but not required.</strong><br data-start=3D"157" data-end=
=3D"160">
=F0=9F=91=89 For a <em data-start=3D"169" data-end=3D"188">first solid mode=
l</em>, I=E2=80=99d start from <strong data-start=3D"205" data-end=3D"214">=
~2022</strong>, then expand if needed.</p>
<p data-start=3D"240" data-end=3D"261">Let me break it down.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"263" data-end=3D"266">
<h2 data-start=3D"268" data-end=3D"317">1=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 What does =E2=
=80=9Cstart from 2020=E2=80=9D actually mean?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"319" data-end=3D"342">From 2020=E2=80=93now you have:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"344" data-end=3D"474">
<li data-start=3D"344" data-end=3D"371">
<p data-start=3D"346" data-end=3D"371">~6 years of hourly data</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"372" data-end=3D"426">
<p data-start=3D"374" data-end=3D"426">6 =C3=97 365 =C3=97 24 =E2=89=88 <st=
rong data-start=3D"389" data-end=3D"424">52,000 time steps per grid cell</s=
trong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"427" data-end=3D"474">
<p data-start=3D"429" data-end=3D"474">Global 0.25=C2=B0 grid (720=C3=97144=
0 after our crop)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"476" data-end=3D"527">That is <strong data-start=3D"484" d=
ata-end=3D"502">a huge dataset</strong>. Good for accuracy, but:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D"641">
<li data-start=3D"529" data-end=3D"563">
<p data-start=3D"531" data-end=3D"563">Training will be <strong data-start=
=3D"548" data-end=3D"563">much slower</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"564" data-end=3D"594">
<p data-start=3D"566" data-end=3D"594">Needs more GPU VRAM and time</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"595" data-end=3D"641">
<p data-start=3D"597" data-end=3D"641">Makes iteration harder (tuning, fixi=
ng bugs)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"643" data-end=3D"646">
<h2 data-start=3D"648" data-end=3D"693">2=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 How much histor=
y do you really <em data-start=3D"686" data-end=3D"692">need</em>?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"695" data-end=3D"755">For short-range weather forecasting =
(what Zeus cares about):</p>
<ul data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D"939">
<li data-start=3D"757" data-end=3D"813">
<p data-start=3D"759" data-end=3D"813">Most useful signal is in the <strong=
 data-start=3D"788" data-end=3D"813">recent climate regime</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"814" data-end=3D"857">
<p data-start=3D"816" data-end=3D"857">The last <strong data-start=3D"825" =
data-end=3D"838">3=E2=80=935 years</strong> are usually enough</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"858" data-end=3D"939">
<p data-start=3D"860" data-end=3D"939">Older data mainly helps with rare ex=
tremes and diversity, not everyday forecast</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"941" data-end=3D"974">You currently have 2020=E2=80=932025=
, so:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"976" data-end=3D"1046">
<li data-start=3D"976" data-end=3D"1046">
<p data-start=3D"978" data-end=3D"1046"><strong data-start=3D"978" data-end=
=3D"991">2022=E2=80=932025</strong> already gives you <strong data-start=3D=
"1010" data-end=3D"1028">3=E2=80=934 full years</strong>, which is plenty.<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1048" data-end=3D"1051">
<h2 data-start=3D"1053" data-end=3D"1084">3=EF=B8=8F=E2=83=A3 Practical rec=
ommendation</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1086" data-end=3D"1121">If I were you, I=E2=80=99d do it l=
ike this:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1123" data-end=3D"1164">=F0=9F=94=B9 Phase 1 =E2=80=93 Ge=
t a good model quickly</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1166" data-end=3D"1203">Train on <strong data-start=3D"117=
5" data-end=3D"1196">recent years only</strong>, e.g.:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1205" data-end=3D"1222">
<li data-start=3D"1205" data-end=3D"1222">
<p data-start=3D"1207" data-end=3D"1222"><strong data-start=3D"1207" data-e=
