<hr data-start=3D"1838" data-end=3D"1841">
<h1 data-start=3D"1843" data-end=3D"1884">=F0=9F=A7=A0 Why PyTorch NGC is t=
he right choice?</h1>
<p data-start=3D"1886" data-end=3D"1913">It automatically gives you:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1915" data-end=3D"2075">
<li data-start=3D"1915" data-end=3D"1930">
<p data-start=3D"1917" data-end=3D"1930">PyTorch 2.x</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1931" data-end=3D"1949">
<p data-start=3D"1933" data-end=3D"1949">CUDA 12.1=E2=80=9312.8</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1950" data-end=3D"1963">
<p data-start=3D"1952" data-end=3D"1963">cuDNN 8.x</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1964" data-end=3D"2008">
<p data-start=3D"1966" data-end=3D"2008">NCCL (multi-GPU comms, but we use =
1 GPU)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2009" data-end=3D"2035">
<p data-start=3D"2011" data-end=3D"2035">AMP enabled by default</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2036" data-end=3D"2075">
<p data-start=3D"2038" data-end=3D"2075">Tensor Float 32 (TF32) acceleratio=
n</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2077" data-end=3D"2098">And most importantly:</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2100" data-end=3D"2180">=E2=9A=A1 <strong data-start=3D"2=
106" data-end=3D"2180">It uses NVIDIA-optimized convolution kernels =E2=86=
=92 2=E2=80=933=C3=97 faster on RTX 4090</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2182" data-end=3D"2235">This speeds up your Zeus UNet trai=
ning significantly.</p>
