<p data-start=3D"847" data-end=3D"953">Adam <strong data-start=3D"852" data=
-end=3D"877">remembers the history</strong> of gradients.<br data-start=3D"=
891" data-end=3D"894">
This history makes training <strong data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"932">fas=
ter</strong> and <strong data-start=3D"937" data-end=3D"952">more stable</s=
trong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"955" data-end=3D"988">If you do NOT save the optimizer:</p=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"990" data-end=3D"1029">=E2=9D=8C You will lose training m=
omentum</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"1030" data-end=3D"1069">=E2=9D=8C Model may overshoot and=
 diverge</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"1070" data-end=3D"1114">=E2=9D=8C Loss will be unstable a=
fter resuming</h3>
<h3 data-start=3D"1115" data-end=3D"1188">=E2=9D=8C Resuming from the middl=
e of training will behave like starting anew</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1190" data-end=3D"1257">By saving <code data-start=3D"1200=
" data-end=3D"1209">"optim"</code>, you resume <strong data-start=3D"1222" =
data-end=3D"1234">smoothly</strong> with correct momentum.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1259" data-end=3D"1292">This is <em data-start=3D"1267" da=
ta-end=3D"1288">extremely important</em> if:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1294" data-end=3D"1405">
<li data-start=3D"1294" data-end=3D"1319">
<p data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1319">You train many epochs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1320" data-end=3D"1351">
<p data-start=3D"1322" data-end=3D"1351">The dataset is large (ERA5)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1352" data-end=3D"1405">
<p data-start=3D"1354" data-end=3D"1405">Variables like precipitation requi=
re 30=E2=80=9350 epochs</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1407" data-end=3D"1410">
<h1 data-start=3D"1412" data-end=3D"1443">=F0=9F=9A=80 <strong data-start=
